There's a difference between learning and mastering.  Learning the game 
in the sense of knowing the commands and rules is easy.  Mastering it, 
i.e. ascending or being able to tell what consequence a given move may 
have in a variety of situations, is not so easy.

Compare it with chess.  It is very easy to learn how to play the game, 
i.e., how to move the pieces.  Winning against a state-of-the art 
program is very difficult however and would mean really mastering the 
game.  In fact, chess is more difficult than nethack in that respect. 
But then, the computer is not really playing *against* you in nethack, 
it is just working the machinery for you...

So I would second the statement "It's a game that's not hard to learn" 
(but still difficult to win...)
